==============================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- THE DISTANCE THEOREM, VERIFIED NUMERICALLY RATHER THAN ASSERTED
==============================================================================================================================
  3140 points, 147 galaxies
  under D x1.37:   max |g_bar ratio - 1| = 6.661e-16     max |1.37 * g_obs ratio - 1| = 4.441e-16
  [PASS] 0A THE DISTANCE THEOREM: g_bar is invariant ROW BY ROW under SPARC's distance rescaling and g_obs picks up exactly the constant 1/f, so a fit that profiles out one offset per galaxy cannot see the distance at all   (g_bar 6.66e-16, g_obs*f 4.44e-16 (machine precision))

==============================================================================================================================
PART 1 -- K1: a_0 FROM THE SHAPE ONLY, AND EVERY NUISANCE LEVER MEASURED
==============================================================================================================================
  SHAPE channel          a_0 = 1.3462e-10   chi^2 = 12583 on 3140 points
  NORMALISATION channel  a_0 = 1.2411e-10   chi^2 = 51641 on the identical points
     vs canonical 9.360e-11: shape +0.158 dex, normalisation +0.123 dex
     vs alt       1.130e-10: shape +0.076 dex, normalisation +0.041 dex
     d log a_0 / d log D        =  SHAPE  +0.0000   NORMALISATION  -2.7367
     d log a_0 / d log sin i    =  SHAPE  +0.0000   NORMALISATION  -5.5279
     d log a_0 / d log cos i    =  SHAPE  +1.4266   NORMALISATION  -1.3374
     d log a_0 / d log Upsilon  =  SHAPE  +1.3631   NORMALISATION  -1.4032
  [PASS] 1A the shape channel is EXACTLY distance-free and exactly free of the sin i that deprojects V_obs, where the normalisation channel -- which is what every existing rung of the a_0 ladder uses -- carries both   (shape d log a_0/d log D = +0.00000, d log a_0/d log sin i = +0.00000; normalisation -2.737 and -5.528)
  [PASS] 1B ⚠ AND INCLINATION IS NOT REMOVED, ONLY HALF OF IT.  The cos i that deprojects the surface brightness multiplies the STELLAR term, sits inside the kernel argument, and is algebraically identical to an Upsilon error.  This check fails if it cancels too -- it does not   (shape d log a_0/d log cos i = +1.427, against d log a_0/d log Upsilon = +1.363 -- the same lever, as the algebra requires)
  [PASS] 1C the shape channel really does contain a_0 -- an interior minimum with a large Delta chi^2 at both ends, not a flat direction dressed as a measurement   (Delta chi^2 = 64822 at 3e-12 and 13556 at 2e-9)
  [PASS] 1D THE NEWTONIAN ALTERNATIVE, computed beside: unboosted baryons must be excluded in this very channel, else the channel is empty   (nu = 1 gives chi^2 = 108970 against 12583 for the kernel, on 3140 points)

==============================================================================================================================
PART 2 -- K1-b / K8(ii): WHERE THE SHAPE LEVERAGE LIVES.  A deep-MOND curve has NO a_0 in its shape.
==============================================================================================================================
  gas-dominated  f_*,loc < 0.25    N=  152 in  17 gal   a_0 = 2.0000e-09  <-- RAILED  lever +0.000   y = 0.016-0.079 (median 0.043)
  star-dominated f_*,loc > 0.90    N= 1615 in  97 gal   a_0 = 1.6362e-10              lever +1.163   y = 0.077-14.062 (median 0.994)
  all SPARC                        N= 3140 in 147 gal   a_0 = 1.3462e-10              lever +1.363   y = 0.029-7.933 (median 0.235)
  [PASS] 2A ⚠ K1 FAILS AS AN M/L-FREE ESTIMATOR, AND THE REASON IS STRUCTURAL.  The gas-dominated subsample -- the only one with a small Upsilon lever -- has no shape leverage at all, because ln g_obs = 1/2 ln g_bar + const there and a constant is exactly what the per-galaxy offset absorbs.  The fit must RAIL.  This check fails if it returns a finite interior minimum   (gas-dominated fit rails at 2.000e-09 (scan bound 2.00e-09); its 95th-percentile y is 0.079, a factor 13 short of the transition)

==============================================================================================================================
PART 3 -- NEW: THE TWO-CHANNEL SOLVE.  Two channels with DIFFERENT Upsilon exponents intersect, and the
           intersection determines a_0 AND Upsilon.  Does the Upsilon it returns exist in nature?
==============================================================================================================================
  shape-channel ridge          a_0 ~ Upsilon^+1.404
  normalisation-channel ridge  a_0 ~ Upsilon^-1.383
  the two ridges CROSS at   Upsilon_[3.6] = 0.487   a_0 = 1.2825e-10
     that a_0 is +0.137 dex from canonical and +0.055 dex from alt
  for reference, the single joint pooled fit (normalisation channel, Upsilon and a_0 both free) sits at Upsilon = 0.575, a_0 = 1.0208e-10, chi^2 = 50251
  ⚠ BUG PATTERN 5, HANDLED EXPLICITLY: a_0 and Upsilon are degenerate inside each channel, so the ridges
     above ARE the degeneracy directions and they are printed rather than hidden.  The solve works only
     because the two exponents differ by 2.79; if they were equal the two channels would
     be one channel and the intersection would not exist.
  [PASS] 3A ⚠ THE TWO-CHANNEL SOLVE RETURNS A STELLAR MASS-TO-LIGHT RATIO THAT MUST EXIST IN NATURE.  Its whole content is that the two channels' Upsilon exponents differ, so their intersection is a measurement.  This check fails if the Upsilon it returns is outside the stellar-population range 0.3-0.8 at 3.6 micron   (Upsilon_[3.6] = 0.487 against SPS 0.5 +- 0.1 (allowed band 0.3-0.8); the two exponents are +1.404 and -1.383, differing by 2.79)
  [PASS] 3B ⚠ AND THE a_0 IT RETURNS MUST LAND ON A FOOTING.  This is the check that decides whether the solve is a measurement of a_0 or only of Upsilon.  It fails if the intersection a_0 sits more than 0.3 dex from both footings   (a_0 = 1.282e-10: +0.137 dex from canonical, +0.055 dex from alt)
  [PASS] 3C ⚠ REPORTED AGAINST INTEREST: the two-channel solve inherits the distance scale from the normalisation channel, so it is NOT distance-free even though half of it is.  This check fails if the combination somehow escaped the distance -- it does not, and the claim must never be made   (the normalisation half carries d log a_0/d log D = -2.737; the combination cannot be cleaner than its dirtiest input)

==============================================================================================================================
PART 4 -- K8: THE STRUCTURAL NO-GO.  Sigma_M = a_0/(2 pi G) against what hydrogen can supply.
==============================================================================================================================
  the surface density at which a thin disc reaches y = 1:  Sigma_M = a_0/(2 pi G) = 106.9 (canonical) / 129.0 (alt) Msun/pc^2
  HI saturates near 10 Msun/pc^2 (above that hydrogen turns molecular): a factor 10.7-12.9 short
  MEASURED IN SPARC: of 2711 points with a positive gas term, the gas-only y has median 0.0225, 99th percentile 0.0991, max 2.9278
  among the 174 GAS-DOMINATED points (local stellar share < 0.25) the max gas-only y is 0.1380
  ⚠ AGAINST INTEREST, THE EXCEPTIONS ARE NAMED: 7 points anywhere in SPARC have a gas-only y > 0.5, all in NGC5005; at those radii the local stellar share is 0.91-0.94, i.e. locally gas-rich but never gas-dominated, so they carry no M/L-free information.
  [PASS] 4A K8(iii) MEASURED: hydrogen cannot put a disc on the transition.  The gas term alone never reaches y ~ 1 in a gas-DOMINATED region of any SPARC galaxy, which is what makes M/L-freedom and shape leverage mutually exclusive.  This check fails if any gas-dominated point reaches y > 0.5   (max gas-only y among gas-dominated points = 0.138; 99th percentile over all gas-bearing points = 0.099)
  [PASS] 4B K8(i) MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED: the trade is exact and neither lever can be small at once.  The shape channel is distance-free and Upsilon-loaded; the normalisation channel is the mirror image   (shape (D +0.0000, Upsilon +1.363) vs normalisation (D -2.737, Upsilon -1.403) -- no channel has both levers small)

==============================================================================================================================
PART 5 -- THE RESTATEMENT TEST, EXECUTED
==============================================================================================================================
  v^4 = G M_b a_0  =>  g_obs^2 = a_0 g_bar  =>  ln g_obs = 1/2 ln g_bar + 1/2 ln a_0.
  The a_0 sits entirely in the ADDITIVE CONSTANT, which is exactly what the per-galaxy offset c_g absorbs.
  So a purely deep-MOND sample must give the shape estimator ZERO leverage.  Executed in PART 2: the
  gas-dominated subsample (y = 0.016-0.079)
  rails at the scan bound with an Upsilon lever of exactly zero -- no Upsilon dependence because no a_0
  dependence.  THE DERIVATION DOES NOT CLOSE: the estimator lives entirely on the TRANSITION, which the
  BTFR does not contain.  is_restatement = False for K1's mechanism.
  ⚠ BUT the thing K1 measures is the same acceleration scale the pooled RAR fit measures, from the same
  147 galaxies, and PART 3 shows the two channels are one two-parameter fit seen along two directions.
  K1 is therefore a NEW ESTIMATOR of an OLD quantity, not a new relation -- it fails hunt criterion (1)
  and (5) is not the reason.

